The current code has a clean seam but no cross-owner mechanism yet: it deliberately computes dereferencing SORT inside the source-owner task and directly reaches other shards only in the one-executor case. The viable extension is a third read wave: source snapshot → arena-owned derived-key plan → owner-grouped gather → one `sort_run` reduction, followed by the existing destination-owner STORE wave. This preserves the pinned snapshot and wall-clock cut without touching MVCC or atomics.
