   858	// The cut a multi-owner READ fragment of this transaction resolves at.  UINT64_MAX means "newest
   859	// committed at the instant this fragment runs", which is what every MULTI child used before this
   860	// lane; that is exactly the behaviour that let one MGET's eight fragments straddle a foreign
   861	// transaction's single ticket.  A transaction that registered no cut (write-only, single-owner, or
   862	// the cut was never drawn) keeps the old value, so nothing else in the file changes shape.
   863	uint64_t multi_read_cut(const MultiExecState& state) {
   864	    return state.snapshot_registered ? state.snapshot : UINT64_MAX;
   865	}
