codex
I also found the transactional seam: cross-shard SORT children already declare all shards as EXEC participants, but their child snapshot is only inherited for read-only commands. `SORT ... STORE` is a write command with a multi-owner read phase, so the implementation must explicitly classify dereferencing SORT as a read-cut consumer and stamp the child from the transaction’s already-pinned cut. That is orchestration-only; the MVCC resolver and atomic record machinery remain untouched.
