tomokv.conf:118:# SORT's BY/GET DEREFERENCE IS PLACEMENT-DEPENDENT, and has no knob of its own.
tomokv.conf:119:# `SORT key BY weight_* GET data_*` names one key per ELEMENT of `key`, and those names are only
tomokv.conf:121:# other owners about them. A shard is touched only by its owning executor, so the dereference is
tomokv.conf:123:# therefore owns every shard. With more than one executor a '*'-bearing BY or GET is refused with
tomokv.conf:124:#   ERR BY option of SORT denied when keys formed by the pattern may be owned by another executor
tomokv.conf:125:# (and the GET spelling), the same shape the reference server uses to refuse the same patterns in
tomokv.conf:126:# cluster mode. Everything that dereferences nothing -- BY with a pattern that has no '*' (which
tomokv.conf:128:# every placement. See NOTES-SORT.md for the design and the options that were rejected.
./NOTES-SORTXSHARD.md:100:- The multi-executor option refusals, `sort_deref_local`, and both denial constants were removed.
